.TH INS 1 "August 2026" "ins 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ins \- a universal CLI package search/install tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ins
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B ins
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ins
is a universal package manager frontend that unifies apt, dnf, pacman,
zypper, flatpak, snap, nix, and apk behind one interface. Sources are
auto-detected by tool presence and ranked by a configurable priority; the
same app from multiple sources is merged into one result.
.PP
Running
.B ins
with no options prints the full command list, grouped by category; every
action takes an explicit flag or subcommand (see below).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ins -s, --search <query>
Search for packages across all sources, deduplicated and ranked.
.TP
.B ins -i, --install <pkg>...
Install one or more packages with confirmation and live progress.
.TP
.B ins -r, --remove <pkg>...
Remove one or more installed packages.
.TP
.B ins -u, --update
Update every detected source's package index, then run detected tool
updaters (pipx, uv, rustup, fwupd) and any custom updaters from the config.
.TP
.B ins -l, --list
List installed packages grouped by source.
.TP
.B ins -o, --outdated
List installed packages with newer versions available.
.TP
.B ins -U, --upgrade <pkg>...
Upgrade one or more installed packages.
.TP
.B ins info <pkg>
Show a detailed view: description, license, homepage, size, install state
per source. Optional inline icons on kitty / iTerm2 / WezTerm.
.TP
.B ins doctor
Scan all sources for duplicate installs and offer to resolve them. Ubuntu
snap-transition stubs (firefox, thunderbird, chromium-browser) are detected
and skipped, and are listed under
.B transition_stubs
in
.B --json
output.
.TP
.B ins export [file]
Write installed packages as a TOML manifest (stdout when no file given).
.TP
.B ins bundle check <file>
Compare a manifest against the installed state; exit non-zero on drift.
.TP
.B ins bundle install <file>
Install what the manifest is missing.
.TP
.B ins history [n]
Show the last n install/remove/upgrade transactions (default 20).
.TP
.B ins undo
Reverse the last install or remove transaction, verifying package state first.
.TP
.B ins completions <bash|zsh|fish|packages> [prefix]
Print a completion script, or package names for dynamic completion
(\fI--installed\fR restricts to installed packages).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --s, --source <source>...
Restrict the action to specific sources (e.g. apt, flatpak, snap).
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Assume yes to all prompts (for scripting).
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output for search, info, list, outdated, bundle check,
doctor, update, history, and dry-run previews.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show what install/remove/update/upgrade would do without changing anything;
with
.BR "ins doctor"
it scans and reports only (no removal prompts).
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Suppress informational output; errors are still shown.
.TP
.B --no-progress
Run actions without the live progress bar.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Print version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives in
.IR ~/.config/ins/config.toml .
.SS Sources
.PP
.B [sources]
.RS
.TP
.B priority = ["apt", "flatpak", ...]
Order used when a package exists in several sources.
.RE
.SS Cache
.PP
.B [cache]
.RS
.TP
.B enabled = true|false
Turn the SQLite cache on or off.
.TP
.B ttl_seconds = 3600
How long cached results stay fresh.
.TP
.B max_entries = 5000
Cache entry cap (oldest entries evicted first).
.RE
.SS Updaters
.PP
.B [updaters]
.RS
.PP
Only the no-password, user-level updaters run by default: pipx, uv, and
rustup.
.TP
.B disable = ["pipx"]
Skip these built-in updaters.
.TP
.B enable = ["fwupd"]
Opt-in updaters. fwupd runs
.BR "fwupdmgr refresh"
(firmware metadata only), which may prompt for admin rights and downloads
firmware metadata, so it is off unless listed here.
.TP
.B custom = { texlive = ["tlmgr", "update", "--all"] }
Extra update commands run by
.BR "ins -u" ;
each is a name mapped to an argv list.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the cache and per-source state
(default
.IR ~/.local/share ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or nothing to do).
.TP
.B 1
A package was not found, or an adapter/updater failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: conflicting actions, unknown source, or bad arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ins/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ins/cache.db
SQLite cache (history, search results, installed state).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
ins -s vlc
Search for VLC across all sources.
.TP
ins -i vlc gimp --dry-run
Preview an install.
.TP
ins -i vlc gimp -y
Install without prompting.
.TP
ins -u
Update indexes and tool updaters.
.TP
ins export bundle.toml && ins bundle check bundle.toml
Provisioning round-trip.
.TP
ins history 5 && ins undo
Review and reverse the last transaction.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR zypper (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR snap (1),
.BR nix-env (1),
.BR apk (8),
.BR pipx (1),
.BR rustup (1),
.BR fwupdmgr (1)
